Testing math floor function (daji):
\nPositive numbers:
  daji(3.8) = 3
  daji(5.1) = 5
  daji(7.999) = 7
\nIntegers:
  daji(5) = 5
  daji(0) = 0
\nNegative numbers:
  daji(-2.4) = -3
  daji(-1.01) = -2
  daji(-5.9) = -6
\nEdge cases:
  daji(0.1) = 0
  daji(-0.1) = -1
  daji(0.999) = 0
\nWith variables:
  x = 4.7
  y = -3.2
  daji(x) = 4
  daji(y) = -4
\nPractical examples:
  50.5 hours = 2 whole days
  27 items with 5 per page = 6 pages
\nMath floor tests completed!
